{"id": "EUVD-2022-56059", "enisaUuid": "12c656fe-c68f-392c-bd34-5d1c7020d8a1", "description": "In FRRouting FRR before 8.5, the service user (usually frr) can escalate its privileges to root by monitoring the configuration directory (/etc/frr) and replacing config files upon creation with, for example, symlinks to change the ownership of arbitrary files. This is a TOCTOU Race Condition caused by a combination of touch and chown.", "datePublished": "2026-09-13T00:00:00", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-14T18:15:19", "baseScore": 6.7, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://bugzilla.suse.com/show_bug.cgi?id=1204124", "https://frrouting.org/security/cve-2022-42917/", "https://github.com/FRRouting/frr/commit/972cdc560e339d70c0ee5fb70ec636ab78f00bca", "https://github.com/FRRouting/frr/compare/frr-8.4...frr-8.5"], "aliases": ["GHSA-x36x-qpcf-qwfj", "CVE-2022-42917"], "assigner": "mitre", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "5d43426c-b0e7-3ddb-b266-637052a39d48", "product": {"name": "FRRouting", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 <4.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9d61829f-073a-3874-b197-9c1a6101a3a9", "vendor": {"name": "FRRouting"}}], "isExploited": false}